I'm always a bit scared when fighting Master Kaen and try not to melee him.
A boulder fort serves well for that purpose. What I found interesting in my
current game was that I used restricted/unskilled +0 darts for that purpose;
after he had been hit by only 16 darts he died. First I meleed those E and X
that passed the boulders from the burnt E-square, then I took each chance to
throw a dart. Initially I zapped sleep at him to keep him in line of missile
file; not sure whether that was effective though, since in the past often I
seem to only miss him with rays. A supporting effect may have had the ring
of conflict, but Kaen was mostly not in close vicinity of the other foes
which I quickly killed with the +6 Grayswandir. I had about 100 of those +0
darts and thought I'd need at least 50 to bring him down. Maybe my gauntlets
of power helped a bit to deal a bit more damage per [single-shot] dart.

